{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1094", "sample_idx": 13, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "```json\n{\n  \"famous_moms\": {\n    \"mom_with_a_mystic_twist\": {\n      \"name\": \"Maya Angelou\",\n      \"claim_to_fame\": \"Poet, memoirist, and civil rights icon who taught us that ‘you may encounter many defeats, but you must not be defeated’—basically the queen of turning heartbreak into a sonnet.\",\n      \"mom_energy\": \"If love and wisdom had a baby, it’d be Maya. She mothered the world with words, healing wounds with rhymes and storytelling that made even the darkest corners feel like a warm kitchen table.\"\n    },\n    \"the_queen_of_quirk\": {\n      \"name\": \"Marilyn Monroe\",\n      \"claim_to_fame\": \"Blonde bombshell, Hollywood royalty, and the original ‘problematic but iconic’ mom figure—she’d probably tell you to ‘give a little, take a little’ while sipping champagne straight from the bottle.\",\n      \"mom_energy\": \"Picture this: Marilyn in a pink satin robe, holding a baby (or a script), saying, ‘Honey, if life gives you lemons, make lemonade—or better yet, be the damn lemonade.’ Chaos with a side of glam.\"\n    },\n    \"the_mathy_mama_bear\": {\n      \"name\": \"Emmy Noether\",\n      \"claim_to_fame\": \"The ‘mother’ of modern algebra and theoretical physics. She’d scold you for not doing your homework *and* prove why your textbook is wrong in one breath. Einstein called her ‘the most significant creative mathematical genius’—your calculus teacher would’ve cried if she dated them.\",\n      \"mom_energy\": \"‘No, sweetie, you can’t just *assume* that E=mc²—let’s derive it over tea and existential dread.’ Her love language? Whiteboards covered in equations and a firm ‘try again, but this time *correctly*.’\"\n    },\n    \"the_feisty_folk_legend\": {\n      \"name\": \"Dolly Parton\",\n      \"claim_to_fame\": \"Country music’s queen, wigs that defy gravity, and a heart bigger than her songwriting credits. She’s the kind of mom who’d build a library for a town *and* write a song about it by breakfast.\",\n      \"mom_energy\": \"‘It takes a lot of money to look this cheap, darlin’—now pass the rhinestones and the hugs.’ Imagine her holding court at a family BBQ, frying up stories like biscuits and serving them with a side of glittery life advice.\"\n    },\n    \"the_witchy_tech_goddess\": {\n      \"name\": \"Ada Lovelace\",\n      \"claim_to_fame\": \"The world’s first computer programmer—she coded before the computer existed. If she were your mom, she’d drag you to the ‘lab’ (aka her parlor) to ‘help’ with her ‘inventions’ (aka glowing eyes and eerie prophecies about the future).\",\n      \"mom_energy\": \"‘My dear, numbers aren’t just for calculations—they’re the language of the universe.’ Picture her muttering about ‘analytical engines’ while knitting sweaters that double as circuits. Spooky but brilliant.\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n```", "logprobs": [{"token": "```", "logprob": -0.0017854715697467327}, {"token": "json", "logprob": -0.00028868322260677814}, {"token": "\n", "logprob": -0.014428215101361275}, {"token": "{\n", "logprob": -0.0038630161434412003}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -0.008278933353722095}, {"token": " \"", "logprob": -0.0036688416730612516}, {"token": "f", "logprob": -0.4429481625556946}, {"token": "amous", "logprob": -0.11968814581632614}, {"token": "_m", "logprob": -0.01926286518573761}, {"token": "oms", "logprob": -0.0246659554541111}, {"token": "\":", "logprob": -0.3432523012161255}, {"token": " {\n", "logprob": -2.239140510559082}, {"token": "   ", "logprob": -0.0002047805901383981}, {"token": " \"", "logprob": -0.00309892650693655}, {"token": "m", "logprob": -1.6601545810699463}, {"token": "om", "logprob": -0.21529412269592285}, {"token": "_with", "logprob": -2.8512966632843018}, {"token": "_a", "logprob": -0.5347075462341309}, {"token": "_m", "logprob": -1.0489027500152588}, {"token": "yst", "logprob": -1.9503722190856934}, {"token": "ic", "